    native_build_mir_entry_sigsegv_cuda_backend_closure_2026-10-10, 0, "2026-11-22 filed from cuda_optimizer_surface_owner_2026_10_10 evidence: 2026-10-10 producer 72b495b3 HIR 157/157 then worker SIGSEGV (exit 139) entering MIR lowering on src/plugins/backend_cuda/cuda_backend.spl closure; SMF path same. Not re-reached on 2026-11-22 (8G MIR OOM / 20G HIR SIGSEGV earlier)."
    native_build_mir_entry_sigsegv_cuda_backend_closure_2026-10-10, 1, "2026-11-26 lane work/bug-cuda-segv-20261126: stage2 ef46f0d2 port_owner closure (includes src/plugins/backend_cuda) at 20G with SIMPLE_PARSE_SHARDING=0 passed HIR 514/514, MIR, and codegen 489/489 without SIGSEGV, then was killed by an external SIGTERM in smf_package. The cuda_backend.spl entry recipe itself has not been re-run on this producer."
    native_build_mir_entry_sigsegv_cuda_backend_closure_2026-10-10, 2, "2026-11-26 own recipe re-run (--entry src/plugins/backend_cuda/cuda_backend.spl --entry-closure, stage2 ef46f0d2, source 847afe06a41, MemoryMax=20G, SIMPLE_PARSE_SHARDING=0 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP=1 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WHOLE_PROGRAM=1, cold caches; flags differ from the 2026-10-10 recipe): worker SIGSEGV (-139, rc 117) at HIR 305/511 (current=compiler.hir.hir_lowering.hir_phase_profile), before MIR; wall 19:21, peak RSS 5.3 GB. apport did not write a new core (crash file still the 17:18 HIR-82 one), so no backtrace for this instance. MIR entry not re-reached; stays open."

